## 3. EVALUATION CRITERIA (weighted)
==============================================================
Evaluate code quality on a scale of **1–10** using the following weighted criteria:

1. Code Readability & Style Consistency  (25 %)
   — Naming conventions, formatting, comments, module structure.

2. Architecture & Abstractions           (25 %)
   — Appropriate use of design patterns, separation of concerns, DRY principle.

3. Error Handling & Robustness           (20 %)
   — Try/except blocks, input validation, edge-case coverage, meaningful error messages.

4. Test Coverage & Quality               (20 %)
   — Presence of unit/integration tests, test quality, assertion depth.

5. Security Considerations               (10 %)
   — No hardcoded secrets, proper input sanitisation, dependency hygiene.

